@bank dept:works
// Pillar 5 Step 3 (head writer W2): team jobs (seat M2), the lead's calls when whoever leads has no line of their own
// (Halloran, Torres and Calder have theirs). Kind 'work', flags team.call.<part>. Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer.
== work
? flag:team.call.start
- Spots, everyone. Wait for your name.
? flag:team.call.brace
- Brace it. Hold there.
? flag:team.call.pass
- Pass it across.
? flag:team.call.hold
- Hold it steady.
? flag:team.call.crank
- Crank. Nice and slow.
? flag:team.call.tip
- Tip it and hold.
? flag:team.call.valves
- The valves. In order.
? flag:team.call.open
- Open them up.
? flag:team.call.drain
- Drain it down.
? flag:team.call.done
- That's it. Good work, everyone.

// the crew chatting while a team job runs (seat X reads kind 'team': one bubble each, 60 characters or fewer)
== team
- Mind your fingers.
- Nearly there.
- Who's got the spanner? Oh. Me.   #funny
- Last time this took two hours.
- My arms are going. Don't tell anyone.   #funny
- Tea after this. I've decided.
- Hear that? That's a happy machine.
- Steady. No rushing in here.
- Is it seated? Properly seated?
- Does anyone know a song for this? No? Fine.   #funny
- Nearly there is my favourite place.
- Four pairs of hands and one spanner. Typical.   #funny
- Careful. It's heavier than it looks.
- Good. That's the hard bit done.
? who:pell
- Is it lunch yet? It feels like lunch.   #funny
? who:kovac-zainab
- Third bolt's a hair loose. Got it.
? who:torres-zeke
- Lovely. Like it was made for it. It was.   #funny
